BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 748.00 Td (06. A patient develops cardiac tamponade. Why can stroke volume fall despite a normal) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 733.30 Td (blood volume?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 714.60 Td (A. Tamponade increases functional ventricular compliance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 699.90 Td (B. Tamponade directly raises venous return above normal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 685.20 Td (C. The aortic valve cannot open due solely to a high heart rate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 670.50 Td (D. High pericardial pressure restricts ventricular filling.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 644.80 Td (07. Arterial pressure inside an arteriole is unchanged, but pressure in its surrounding) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 630.10 Td (tissue rises. What happens to transmural pressure?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 611.40 Td (A. It decreases because the pressure difference narrows.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 596.70 Td (B. It increases because the pressure difference widens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 582.00 Td (C. It becomes identical to intravascular arterial pressure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 567.30 Td (D. It remains fixed because arterial pressure is unchanged.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 541.60 Td (08. A severely underperfused patient begins breathing rapidly, although the lungs were) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 526.90 Td (initially healthy. What drives this change?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 508.20 Td (A. Increased aerobic ATP production stimulates breathing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 493.50 Td (B. Suppression of the peripheral chemoreceptors stimulates breathing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 478.80 Td (C. Lactic acidosis stimulates peripheral chemoreceptors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 464.10 Td (D. High tissue oxygen content increases respiratory drive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.1 Tf 47 438.40 Td (09. How does local hypoxia affect most systemic arterioles versus pulmonary arterioles?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 419.70 Td (A. Systemic vessels constrict while pulmonary vessels dilate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 405.00 Td (B. Both primarily constrict to lower oxygen delivery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 390.30 Td (C. Both remain relatively insensitive to tissue oxygen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.1 Tf 62 375.60 Td (D. Systemic vessels dilate; pulmonary vessels constrict.) Tj ET
